`neutron dev` runs `air` when it is installed, otherwise `go run ./cmd/server`.
The server connects to the database at startup and exits if it cannot.

## Endpoints

- `GET /api/hello` — sample route in `internal/handler/hello.go`
- `GET /health` — built in: `{"status", "nucleus", "version"}`

## Configuration

Read from the environment (`.env.example` lists them; nothing loads it automatically):

| Variable | Default |
|---|---|
| `NEUTRON_HOST` / `NEUTRON_PORT` | listen on `:8080` |
| `NEUTRON_DATABASE_URL` | then `DATABASE_URL`, then `postgres://localhost:5432/{{.Name}}` |
| `NEUTRON_LOG_LEVEL` | `info` |
